[264] indent=0 block=-
[265] indent=10 block=36bdbe27
      "▾ "
      "Good"
[266] indent=12 block=36bdbe27
      "Question:" {b}
      " "
[267] indent=0 block=-
[268] indent=12 block=36bdbe27
      "\"For ERCOT operating day 2026-05-15, why are LMPs forecast " {i}
[269] indent=12 block=36bdbe27
      "so low in DA at HB_WEST?\"" {i}
[270] indent=0 block=-
[271] indent=12 block=36bdbe27
      "Response: " {b}
[272] indent=0 block=-
[273] indent=12 block=36bdbe27
      "“The short answer: a classic West Texas renewable oversupply" {i}
[274] indent=12 block=36bdbe27
      "event. Strong southerly winds combined with robust solar " {i}
[275] indent=12 block=36bdbe27
      "irradiance during daylight hours pushed generation well " {i}
[276] indent=12 block=36bdbe27
      "above local load, creating significant negative-price hours " {i}
[277] indent=12 block=36bdbe27
      "in the DA market.\n[Followed by a DA vs. RT price table " {i}
[278] indent=12 block=36bdbe27
      "covering HE9–HE18 across HB_WEST, HB_NORTH, and HB_HOUSTON, " {i}
[279] indent=12 block=36bdbe27
      "then three drivers: wind, solar, transmission congestion]" {i}
[280] indent=0 block=-
[281] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "\nHB_WEST was negative or near-zero for 10 consecutive hours " {i}
[282] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "(HE9–HE18 CDT), while HB_NORTH and HB_HOUSTON were clearing " {i}
[283] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "$14–$38/MWh during the same window. That's a massive basis " {i}
[284] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "spread driven by local congestion.”" {i}
[285] indent=0 block=-
[286] indent=10 block=36bdbe27
      "▾ "
      "Bad"
[287] indent=12 block=36bdbe27
      "Question:" {b}
      " "
[288] indent=0 block=-
[289] indent=12 block=36bdbe27
      "\"For ERCOT operating day 2026-05-15, which Load Zone is " {i}
[290] indent=12 block=36bdbe27
      "forecasted to have the highest peak load, and which hours?\"" {i}
[291] indent=0 block=-
[292] indent=12 block=36bdbe27
      "Response:" {b}
[293] indent=0 block=-
[294] indent=12 block=36bdbe27
      "“The load profiles are charted above. NORTH_ERCOT's " {i}
[295] indent=12 block=36bdbe27
      "dominance is clear throughout the day, with the gap widening" {i}
[296] indent=12 block=36bdbe27
      "significantly from HE14 onward into the evening peak. Let me" {i}
[297] indent=12 block=36bdbe27
      "know if you want to cross-reference with RT actuals or DA " {i}
[298] indent=12 block=36bdbe27
      "prices for that zone.”" {i}
[299] indent=0 block=-
[300] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "Reviewer Comment:" {b}
[301] indent=0 block=-
[302] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "“No chart outputted. The answer never states which zone has " {i}
[303] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "the highest peak load or which hours. \"NORTH_ERCOT's " {i}
[304] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "dominance is clear throughout the day\" implies it's the " {i}
[305] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "answer, but the question asked for a specific zone and " {i}
[306] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "specific hours. neither is stated explicitly. A reader who " {i}
[307] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "needs this for a DA bid can't act on \"dominance is clear.””" {i}
[308] indent=0 block=-
