      "Good"
[331] indent=12 block=36bdbe27
      "Question:" {b}
[332] indent=0 block=-
[333] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "\"How did ERCOT real-time prices settle relative to DA " {i}
[334] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "forecasts by hub on 2026-05-15?”" {i}
[335] indent=0 block=-
[336] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "Response:" {b}
[337] indent=0 block=-
[338] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "Here's the DA vs. RT settlement picture for May 15." {i}
[339] indent=0 block=-
[340] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "Key themes:" {b i}
[341] indent=0 block=-
[342] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "West/Panhandle — RT ran well above DA overnight, then " {b i}
[343] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "flipped" {b i}
      "\nHB_WEST and HB_PAN were the most notable deviations. " {i}
[344] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "RT beat DA by $17–19/MWh in the overnight hours (HE1–HE8), " {i}
[345] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "likely reflecting lower-than-forecast wind output when DA " {i}
[346] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "priced in strong generation. Both hubs then flipped negative" {i}
[347] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "in the evening (HE19–HE20) before spiking again at " {i}
[348] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "HE22–HE24." {i}
[349] indent=0 block=-
[350] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "South — persistent RT discount through the afternoon" {b i}
      "\nHB_SOUTH" {i}
[351] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "was the weakest performer relative to DA. RT ran $10–15/MWh " {i}
[352] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "below DA from HE10 through HE16 — solar likely overperformed" {i}
[353] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "DA expectations, suppressing real-time prices. The daily " {i}
[354] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "average gap was -$5.48/MWh, the largest negative DART of any" {i}
[355] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "hub." {i}
[356] indent=0 block=-
[357] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "Houston — RT outperformed DA in the afternoon peak" {b i}
      "\nHB_HOUSTON" {i}
[358] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "was the only load-zone hub to finish the day with a positive" {i}
[359] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "DART (+$0.93/MWh). The afternoon ramp (HE15–HE18) saw RT " {i}
[360] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "exceed DA by up to $14.52/MWh, pointing to tighter supply " {i}
[361] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "conditions in the Houston pocket than the DA anticipated." {i}
[362] indent=0 block=-
[363] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "North — roughly flat on the day" {b i}
      "\nHB_NORTH tracked DA closely, " {i}
[364] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "with a modest -$0.87/MWh daily average. The afternoon hours " {i}
[365] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "showed mild RT premiums, but midday solar suppression offset" {i}
[366] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "those gains." {i}
[367] indent=0 block=-
