      "└──────┴────────────┴──────┴───────────────────────────────┘" {fg=#9b9a97}
[399] indent=0 block=-
[400] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "What this tells you about DA bid behavior:" {b i}
[401] indent=0 block=-
[402] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "• "
      "The " {i}
      "midday DA premium (HE9–HE13)" {b i}
      " — up to $8.21 at HE12 — " {i}
[403] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "is consistent with bidders pricing in solar uncertainty. " {i}
[404] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "DA cleared well above where RT settled, suggesting the " {i}
[405] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "market priced a risk premium for afternoon solar " {i}
[406] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "variability that didn't materialize as severely in RT." {i}
[407] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "• "
      "The " {i}
      "HE15–HE17 reversal" {b i}
      " (RT > DA by up to $8.70) points to " {i}
[408] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "an underestimation of the evening ramp in DA — the " {i}
[409] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "opposite effect, where RT tightened faster than DA " {i}
[410] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "anticipated." {i}
[411] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "• "
      "DAM volumes" {b i}
      " show buy-side demand peaking in HE17–HE22 " {i}
[412] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "(~17,500–18,300 MWh) with sell-side heaviest in HE9–HE13 " {i}
[413] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "(~5,000–5,300 MWh), consistent with participants locking " {i}
[414] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "in DA sales during the solar window." {i}
[415] indent=0 block=-
[416] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────" {fg=#9b9a97}
[417] indent=0 block=-
[418] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "If you're working with a specific model or framework that " {i}
[419] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "uses \"uncertainty penalization\" as a defined term — e.g., a " {i}
[420] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "stochastic bidding model or a specific EQ methodology — let " {i}
[421] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "me know and I can pull the relevant context. I can also " {i}
[422] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "break this down by node-level prices within the North zone " {i}
[423] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "if the hub view isn't granular enough." {i}
[424] indent=0 block=-
[425] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "Reviewer Comment:" {b}
[426] indent=0 block=-
[427] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "This response erodes my confidence in the chatbot. Question " {i}
[428] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "2 was nearly the same; but generated this response:\nNo " {i}
[429] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "strategy run data found for ERCOT operating day 2026-05-15 " {i}
[430] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "at HB_NORTH." {i}
[431] indent=0 block=-
[432] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "I see how this response (likely) doesn't rely on bid data at" {i}
[433] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "all, and just uses DART trends to speak at a high level " {i}
[434] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "about expected bidding behavior. But that doesn't answer the" {i}
[435] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "question of \"how did\", it answers the question \"how could\"." {i}
[436] indent=0 block=-
[437] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "\nAdditionally, it's unclear if the data referenced in the " {i}
[438] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "response is forecast or actuals." {i}
[439] indent=0 block=-
[440] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "\nIf actuals: this response is not helpful, as it doesn't " {i}
[441] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "include any aspect of uncertainty." {i}
[442] indent=0 block=-
[443] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "\nIf forecasts: a point forecast is always an estimate, but it" {i}
[444] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "doesn't capture uncertainty. What is the agent using to " {i}
[445] indent=12 block=36cdbe27
      "identify uncertainty?" {i}
[446] indent=0 block=-
